Using a traditional Java class, we have to manually define a constructor, getters, equals(),
     hashCode(), and toString() methods. A record automatically provides all of these,
     reducing redundancy and improving maintainability.

    No Boilerplate Code – No need to write constructors, getters, equals(), hashCode(), or toString().
    Immutable by Default – Ensures safety for read-only data.
    Built-in equals() & hashCode() – Avoids duplicate student records.